Yes, this was actually my question. I think giants should be able to 
pick up a boulder directly by moving on the square where it is.  The 
problem is then for the game how to provide this capability.  What 
happens when you go to the square of a boulder as a giant is that you 
just push it as everyone else.  Only if you can't move it, you get a 
different effect, which is not that you squeeze into a space close to 
tha boulder as it would be for a human, elf or orc who does not carry 
too much stuff.  The message that you get is that you push the boulder 
aside easily (or s.th. similar).  You can carry as much stuff as you 
like.  Then you are on the square of the boulder and can just pick it 
up.  It opens a new category in your inventory:  boulders/statues.  So 
technically, you do not *squeeze* into the boulder size.  Therefore, 
technically, you might also not be penalized.  But as I take from the 
post by Boudewijn, this is an irrelevant question, since you will not be 
able to pick up a boulder as a giant in Sokoban.  So I guess, you also 
will get the squeezing message there rather than the "push aside" one.
